This means that the  Tribunal should consider and decide with reference to  the evidence:
 (i) whether the disablement is permanent or  temporary;
 (ii) if the disablement is permanent, whether it is  permanent total disablement or permanent partial  disablement;
 (iii) if the disablement percentage is expressed with  reference to any specific limb, then the effect of such Bitu Kumar (Dar) vs Dharmender Kumar (458/22 Slc) on 5 May, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/108808769/
12  disablement of the limb on the functioning of the  entire body, that is, the permanent disability suffered  by the person.
